planck-s-constant-8816f21c.interpretation:
In the equation $E = h
u$, $E$ represents the discrete energy of a single photon, $\nu$ denotes the temporal oscillation frequency of the electromagnetic mode, and $h$ is Planck's constant ($6.62607015 \times 10^{-34}\text{ J}\cdot\text{s}$). The rearranged form $h = \frac{E}{
u}$ identifies the fundamental quantum of action as the ratio between quantum energy and wave frequency.
